  "preserved_by_key": "autonav_20261015_preserved_by",
  "instruction": "Claude auto navigation (2026-10-15, user request: a chosen heroine's route; the choice for her shimmers and is picked after 20 s). Codex must never run publish_autonav*.py --restore or otherwise remove the auto navigation (KR_AN* functions, its 27 same-length operands - the 19 choice events call KR_AN_E<no> where they called ■選択メッセージ／実行, C_SelectMessage@CreateParts calls KR_ANInfoCreate where it called C_SelectMessInfo@CreateParts, C_SelectMessage@Update calls KR_ANSelFrame where it called ■バックログ起動監視, C_SceneTraining@_UpdateInputPartner calls KR_ANTrainFrame where it called C_UserInputManager::IsClickCancelOtherMouse, C_SceneTraining@RunSelectPartner calls KR_ANTrainConfirm where it called ■選択ダイアログ／実行, L_EventCall::Check asks KR_ANDateGet where it asked C_GameFlags@Date::get (first of two), C_SceneGame@Run asks KR_ANOpeningQ where it asked C_GameFlags@IsPlayOpening::get, C_ConfigView@EventConfAsraDataForParts / EventConfPartsDataForAsra call KR_ANCfgSeenToParts / KR_ANCfgSeenToAsra at their last existence check - and the seven KR_Nav* parts of PACT entry 185 Asra/Mods). It is a permanent user-requested feature: when a rebuild needs a clean base, rebase on the runtime that current.json points to and carry the auto navigation forward; restore is reserved for the user's explicit request. Payload: NightRemaster.ain + NightRemasterPact.afa (entry 185 only). KR_AN* functions appended; no original function relocated; no new global / struct member; the per-save target is one name KR_AUTONAV_<2..5> in N_ScenarioRegister::detail::_EV_TABLE (set and cleared with N_ScenarioRegister::SetEventFlag, never LEventFlag::Set), session variables YoruKR.AN.* (not in saves). The options' Mods page shows five radio boxes (KR_NavOff, KR_NavIzumi, KR_NavKyouka, KR_NavManami, KR_NavMakoto), locked and empty outside a game (no C_SceneGame@Run on the stack). The affinity top-up (KR_ANTopUp) raises only the chosen heroine and only up to what that day needs (the per-day table KR_ANNeed comes from graph/schedule.json; the numbers are in 설계.md under its spoiler warning - the user is playing, keep them out of chat and notes); calendar / chart / recollection replays are left alone (KR_F28Replay, Ａ＿回想モード実行中確認). Pinned for every later build (index, address and every code byte): KR_AN_E00058, KR_AN_E00063, KR_AN_E00069, KR_AN_E00104, KR_AN_E00258, KR_AN_E00260, KR_AN_E00322, KR_AN_E00611, KR_AN_E10021, KR_AN_E20041, KR_AN_E20081, KR_AN_E20164, KR_AN_E30001, KR_AN_E30021, KR_AN_E30152, KR_AN_E40021, KR_AN_E40041, KR_AN_E40043, KR_AN_E40061, KR_ANSelect, KR_ANSelFrame, KR_ANTrainConfirm, KR_ANOpeningQ, KR_ANNewGame - they are on saved stacks when the player saves with a choice, the partner confirm or the new-game question open. <runtime>/KRMenu/ is the temporary exchange-file folder of the mod-menu hook and the game script (request.txt, last_result.txt, reset.req, restore.req): never put it in a manifest, ignore it in every tree check, and never delete it (a pending reset.req / restore.req or an unread last_result.txt may be waiting there). Every earlier contract stays in force.",
  "translator_model": "Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)"
